note long_alias: names that share their first 8 bytes are different names. counter_a, counter_b and the
note 8-byte counter_ hold 20, 1 and 100, so the result is 20 + 1 + 100 - 100 = 21. A compiler that kept
note only the first 8 bytes would make them one name holding 100 and exit 200 (the mutants of seed/omc/gate-longnames.sh).
fn main to int
counter_a = int 20
counter_b = int 1
counter_ = int 100
ret sub add add counter_a counter_b counter_ 100
end
